Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.

About the Role &nbsp;

Voyager is Anduril’s modular, rugged suite of&nbsp;compute, networking, and communications built for survivable C5ISR at the tactical edge - a TRL-9, globally fielded portfolio spanning roughly 75 products, from body-worn gateways to high-performance compute clusters, shipping at industrial scale (tens of thousands of units per year).&nbsp;It’s&nbsp;the hardware backbone of our “Own the Edge” strategy: the compute and connectivity every service runs on. &nbsp;

We’re hiring a Senior Sales &amp; Capture Manager to own Voyager revenue as an individual contributor - a hunter who can carry a number, shape and win captures across the DoW, and pull Voyager through the programs where Anduril is already winning. You’ll operate across all US services (Army, USMC, USAF, SOCOM, Navy), working prime and subcontractor paths, and sell the system - compute, network, comms, chassis, and Lattice attach - not the box. &nbsp;

This is a quota-carrying, deal-closing role for someone who thrives in a fast-moving, high-ambiguity environment and wants to put hardware in the hands of warfighters at scale. &nbsp;

What Y ou’ll Do &nbsp;

• Own a Voyager bookings/ACV target across DoW accounts - build and manage the pipeline end to end, from qualification through close. &nbsp;

• Run captures on programs of record and emerging opportunities: shape requirements, build win strategies, price to win, and quarterback proposals with BD, product, and program teams. &nbsp;

• Drive pull-through:&nbsp;attach Voyager to Anduril’s flagship wins (NGC2, TITAN, USMC C2 modernization, SBMC) and to command-post, vehicle, and dismounted-operator use cases. &nbsp;

• Sell the full stack - position Voyager HPC/VM/VMm&nbsp;compute, G1/TRX/ESR networking and comms, and chassis/integration solutions as an integrated mission system, and drive Lattice software attach. &nbsp;

• Build and own senior relationships across program offices, PEOs, primes, and integration partners (e.g., Palantir, Microsoft, HPE, L3Harris,&nbsp;Viasat). &nbsp;

• Navigate defense acquisition: OTAs, IDIQs, sole-source and competitive vehicles, and the FYDP/POM cycle. &nbsp;

• Bring the field back inside - feed customer requirements, pricing pressure, and competitive intel to product and pricing so Voyager stays ahead. &nbsp;

• Represent Voyager at service events, demos, and exercises; translate hard tech into warfighter outcomes. &nbsp;

What W e’re Looking For &nbsp;

• 8+ years selling or capturing complex hardware/technical solutions to the DoW, with a track record of closing multi-million-dollar deals and hitting quota. &nbsp;

• Deep familiarity with at least one US service’s acquisition ecosystem, and the ability to&nbsp;operate&nbsp;across several. &nbsp;

• Command of technical products - comfortable going deep on rugged compute, tactical networking,&nbsp;SWaP&nbsp;tradeoffs, and C5ISR concepts, and translating them for both operators and acquisition stakeholders. &nbsp;

• Demonstrated capture leadership: win strategy, teaming, price-to-win, and proposal orchestration on competitive pursuits. &nbsp;

• Strong existing relationships across program offices, primes, and/or systems integrators. &nbsp;

• Willingness to travel heavily (50%+) to customer sites,

